      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for checking that. i actually double checked the bucket name and it matches exactly. i also checked the bucket policy and it doesn't seem to have any Deny statements in it. \n\nwait i just noticed something in my resource line. i have \"arn:aws:s3:::my-app-logs-bucket\" but should it be different for PutObject? i thought i needed to specify the objects inside the bucket too?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You are correct; for `s3:PutObject`, you generally do **not** need to specify the key name (e.g., `my-logs/error.log`) directly in the `Resource` field if `s3:PutObject` is the action.\nUsing the bucket ARN without a slash at the end (`arn:aws:s3:::my-app-logs-bucket`) is the correct syntax for allowing the Lambda to write *any* object within that bucket.\nThe slash before the key (`arn:aws:s3:::my-app-logs-bucket/some-key`) is only required if you intend to restrict permissions to specific files or prefixes inside the bucket.",
      "source": "target",
